! Journal

[[GitHub Repository|https://github.com/mblackman/tiddlywiki-journal]] · [[Live Demo|https://mblackman.github.io/tiddlywiki-journal/]]

Structured daily, weekly, monthly, and yearly journaling and habit tracking for TiddlyWiki. Log daily activities, habits, wins, challenges, and gratitude in a structured format that automatically rolls up into weekly, monthly, and annual review views.

!! Features

* ''Structured Entries'': Dedicated templates for Daily (`YYYY-MM-DD`), Weekly (`GGGG-[W]WW`), Monthly (`YYYY-MM`), and Yearly (`YYYY`) journal entries.
* ''Configurable Habit Tracking'': Track numeric, checkbox, and text habits per day with visual habit dots on calendar grids and automatic summary tables across weeks, months, and years.
* ''Hierarchical Roll-Ups'': Daily highlights, wins, gratitude lists, and challenges automatically roll up into Weekly, Monthly, and Yearly reviews.
* ''Quick Access'': Includes a ''Journal'' sidebar tab, a page controls toolbar button, and a ''Journal Dashboard'' (`$:/plugins/mblackman/journal/dashboard`) with 1-click tiles for Today, Week, Month, Year, date jumping, and recent entries.
* ''Built-in Day.js Engine'': Includes Day.js (with `isoWeek` and `advancedFormat`) out of the box via both the `<<dayjs>>` macro and `[dayjs[...]]` filter operator — no external date plugin required.
* ''Media Integration'': Optional integration with [[Media Importer|$:/plugins/mblackman/media-importer]] (`https://github.com/mblackman/tiddlywiki-media-importer`) for logging daily media consumption.

!! Date Formatting Helpers

* ''Filter Operator'': `{{{ [[2026-10-23]dayjs[GGGG-[W]WW]] }}}` or `{{{ [[now]dayjs[YYYY-MM-DD]] }}}`
* ''Macro'': `<<dayjs "2026-10-23" "GGGG-[W]WW">>` (defaults to today and `YYYY-MM-DD` when omitted)
